Subject: [PATCH] library: the Library's text for Claude reaches the sessions
 magpie hosts (#5445)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Library -> Instructions writes its shared text into ~/.claude/CLAUDE.md,
but magpie's own managed Claude spawns run with --setting-sources ""
on purpose (the host's settings and the claude-cli:// handler stay out,
#4928) — so the one agent the Library was on for never read it, and the
Library could not deliver to the very sessions magpie hosts (#5445,
luzhuang: the session's system.md held none of the text, A/B with the
flag).

The sync keeps a snapshot of the text it wrote for Claude beside
library.json (instructions-claude.md, removed when the instructions go
off), and a Claude run carries that snapshot the way a caller's own
instructions ride --append-system-prompt-file: before them when a run
has both, alone when it has none. The isolation is untouched — nothing
of the host's is read; the gateway reads the snapshot by path
(settings.Dir() is shared ground), so the hot path takes no library
dependency.

